 we should respond to James Carter's initial statement (which we haven't seen but we have his content in the system). Actually the system gave us James Carter's round 1 content: He recommended Candidate D with reasoning. So we need to respond to that. We can either agree, challenge, or add nuance. We have our own notes. We should incorporate our own facts. We can either support D or propose another candidate. According to our own notes, we have similar facts. We could agree with D but raise concerns about crew cooperation, maybe ask for more info. But we need to produce a public message with a vote. We can either vote D or another. Let's decide: maybe we can support D but ask for clarification on crew cooperation. However we need to give a vote. We could vote D as well. That aligns with James. That would be consistent. Provide evidence: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, respond to unexpected events. Also note concerns: know-it-all, hot temper. Compare with others. That matches James's points. So we can agree and reinforce. Provide a concise argument.\n\nThus public message: I agree with James, recommend D, explain why, compare.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate D.\n\nProceed."}
